## Single-Atom Catalysts
Less is more: A photocatalyst comprising atomically dispersed Co in an extended MOF efficiently reduces ${\mathsf{C O}}_{2}$ . Directional migration of photogenerated excitons from porphyrin to catalytic cobalt centers was witnessed, thereby supplying longlived electrons for reduction of ${\mathsf{C O}}_{2}$ molecules adsorbed on cobalt centers.
